Include <stdlib.h> in demumble's vendored swift Demangler.h, which calls malloc() and free().

Build fix, not a runtime bug: with the wasi-sdk 34 libc++ nothing else in the include chain
declares malloc, so Demangler.cpp fails to compile ("use of undeclared identifier 'malloc'");
a host build (clang++ with libstdc++) picks it up transitively. No test: there is no runtime
behaviour to test, the build is the check. Not fixed in demumble as of 10e00fb, which is both
bloaty's submodule pin and demumble HEAD on 2026-11-21; swift's own Demangler.h (swiftlang/swift
main) still has no direct include either.
Upstream: none found (nico/demumble and google/bloaty issues/PRs searched 2026-11-21).

diff --git a/third_party/demumble/third_party/swift/include/swift/Demangling/Demangler.h b/third_party/demumble/third_party/swift/include/swift/Demangling/Demangler.h
--- a/third_party/demumble/third_party/swift/include/swift/Demangling/Demangler.h
+++ b/third_party/demumble/third_party/swift/include/swift/Demangling/Demangler.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #define SWIFT_DEMANGLING_DEMANGLER_H
 
 #include "swift/Demangling/Demangle.h"
 #include "swift/Demangling/NamespaceMacros.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 //#define NODE_FACTORY_DEBUGGING
